what's going on guys this is rob and  it's been a long  time since we did the beyond omega level  series and so in this video we're going  to tackle a character that some of you  guys may be aware of but a lot of you  guys been asking for  especially after we did the video on the  spectre so long ago we're talking about  eclipso so eclipsa was first created by  bob haney and lee elias and made his  first appearance in house of secrets  number 61 in 1963. you know that's an  old comic book that's a very old comic  book i feel like i'm gonna have to buy  that old comic book you know where i'm  gonna go to buy that old comic book i'm  gonna go to hip ecommerce yes i am  okay here's the thing about hip  ecommerce i love these guys i had a  phone call with him i was talking to him  the whole idea behind hip ecommerce is  yes  it's a place where you can buy and sell  comics but their motivation is what got  me into it so basically the goal here is  to  help local comic book stores survive in  the digital age by not only selling  their stuff  in local shops but also selling it  online and the best thing about this  it was built for collectors by  collectors that's what really got me  into it because as you guys know  i collect old school comics to top all  it off they have regular auctions  and they have regular sales so you can  go on there and get some ridiculously  good deals and stuff  i went on there and bought some stuff i  loved it but make sure you guys check  out the link down in the description  make sure you go sign up for hip  ecommerce and make sure you buy some  comics but back into our video at the  time of his creation  eclipso was really not depicted as being  a major threat and he was really just a  b-list villain of the week just to give  superheroes somebody to beat up on right  you guys remember  how it was or maybe you don't remember  but you've read about how it was back in  the 1960s so originally eclipsa was the  alter ego of scientist bruce gordon who  traveled to the jungle to observe a  solar eclipse when he encountered a  sorcerer named mophir who attacked bruce  and cut him with a black diamond now the  result of this is that any time there  was an eclipse  gordon was transformed into the super  villain eclipso who had pretty generic  power super strength increased  durability and energy blast from his  eyes and he remained this way in sort of  a jekyll and hyde situation between  bruce gordon and eclipso until 1992 when  the character got his own mini-series  called the darkness within  by robert lauren fleming and keith  giffen and what this mini-series did was  drastically alter the origin and powers  of eclipso it was revealed that the  black diamond that wounded bruce  gordon in the jungle was actually a  shard of a black diamond called the  heart of darkness now in the late 1800s  the way we were told this anyway  a treasure hunter had found the black  diamond and took it to a jeweler to cut  into a thousand pieces which had the  effect  of weakening the bonds that were  trapping the soul of a demon inside  and so when bruce gordon was cut by a  shard of the heart of darkness  eclipso's soul was able to escape and  possess him and it was further revealed  that he was simply pretending to be a  somewhat lame supervillain so as not to  draw the attention of earth's  superheroes  as well as sabotage gordon's research  into solar energy as solar energy is his  primary weakness and he feared the  development of a weapon that could  harness that energy and use it against  him and so it's during this mini-series  that we learned not only that eclipso  can possess others who touch one of the  thousands shards of the black diamond  but that he can also absorb the mass and  powers of others and can also use the  anger of others to create  literal monsters now eclipso's origin  was given yet  another vision in john ostringer's  spectre series in the 1990s for those of  you guys who saw  the beyond omega level video on the  spectre this will all sound super  familiar but for those of you guys who  don't know the spectre was depicted as  the embodiment of the wrath of god but  as it turns out he was not the first to  hold that position and in fact he took  it over from eclipso meaning that  eclipso was in fact  divine in origin now once dc launched  the new 52 in 2011  eclipso's origin was completely  retconned but because this is not the  version of the character that's most  powerful we're not going to focus on his  character in this video but  basically his whole origin is tied to  gem world instead of being a divine  being yeah  it sucks you're not wrong for believing  that it does but as for cubs those  powers they are  really quite vast like i said earlier he  possesses superhuman strength as well as  superhuman speed and stamina he's  practically  invulnerable to damage and being divine  in nature is effectively immortal he  possesses the power of flight and can  produce  powerful energy blasts from his eyes but  each of his eyes actually emits a  different  sort of energy his left eye produces  rays of dark light that are fatal to its  victims and the black light from his  right eye paralyzes opponents when it  passes through a shard of the black  diamond now klypso is also able to  possess others and when doing so he's  able to manipulate their emotions  memories and powers he can augment their  existing powers or even grant them new  powers now while this ability was  originally limited to only individuals  who physically touched a shard of the  heart of darkness  it was later made clear that eclipso's  possession powers work  even when he's far away from them  eclipso was able to corrupt the  individuals he possesses making their  darkest thoughts and desires  too strong to resist and can even alter  their physical appearance  as he did with hawkman and commissioner  gordon in the darkness within  many series now his ability to possess  others extends to extremely powerful and  intelligent individuals as well  as he possessed batman shazam and  superman during that event  now there have been more than one  instance in which eclipso has  demonstrated abilities that are beyond  omega level for instance  one of eclipso's powers is his ability  to absorb the mass and powers of others  and he was able to do this to the  spectre  and so if you're familiar with the  spectre at all you'll know that he's one  of the most powerful characters in dc  comics so for klipso to be able to  absorb his powers  definitely gives him the potential to be  beyond omega level since the spectrum  himself is well beyond  omega level in that way now on one  occasion calypso used his vast power  to control the very forces of nature and  caused a solar eclipse that shrouded the  entire world in darkness  obviously the ability to cut off the  earth from its light source for an  extended period of time  could make the entire planet  uninhabitable meaning eclipso is a  potential planetary threat and on a very  famous occasion probably the most famous  occasion eclipso  almost did destroy all life on earth as  it was actually him that was responsible  for the great flood  as in like the flood from the bible that  we get in noah's ark story and so  eclipso  acting as the embodiment of god's wrath  at that time sought to punish mankind  for their evil deeds so he sent a flood  that covered the entire world  and killed everyone but the people on  that arc so  because we know eclipso can wield divine  powers efficient enough to destroy a  world we can comfortably place him  in the omega level or beyond omega level  tier but let me know what you guys think  down below let me know in the comments  section what characters you guys want to  see  covered in future series make sure you  guys check out hip ecommerce  and i will catch you all later peace
 

